# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build context whitelist for the OMICohort image.
#
# EXCLUDE EVERYTHING, then re-include only what the running app opens. The
# working tree is ~19 GB and the app needs ~1.76 GB of it; the rest is pipeline
# input (data/raw/tcga_* alone is 14 GB), download caches, prior-state archives
# and backups. A blacklist would have to be updated every time the tree grows a
# directory, and the failure mode is silent: the image just gets bigger.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT TRUSTED ON ITS OWN. Docker's re-include rules are subtle
# enough that a wrong pattern here would drop a file the app needs and the
# image would still build. `scripts/docker_selfcheck.R` runs inside the build
# and fails it by name if anything required is missing -- see the Dockerfile.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*

# ---- code, configuration, assets ----
# R/ is listed FILE BY FILE, matching .gitignore exactly. The other 23 files in R/ are CLI
# pipeline drivers outside app.R's source() closure; 10 of them hard-code an absolute home
# directory. Copying them in would put those paths inside a published image, and -- the
# reason this is worth the twelve lines -- would make an image built HERE differ from one
# built from a clone, which is the property `docker build` is supposed to guarantee.
!.Rprofile
!app.R
!R
R/*
!R/about.R
!R/brand.R
!R/cptac.R
!R/data_access.R
!R/depmap.R
!R/guide.R
!R/plots.R
!R/registry.R
!R/rppa.R
!R/scan_lookup.R
!R/survival_engine.R
!R/tumor_normal.R
!config
config/*.bak_*
# Prior-state archives of the registry (config/archive_pre_colonpanel/ shipped in 0.1.7 and
# 0.1.8 because the line above matches only the top level). Step 287.
config/archive_*
!www
!scripts/docker_selfcheck.R

# ---- feature matrices, clinical database, RPPA tables ----
# Everything the app can open lives at the top level of data/processed as
# <kind>_<cohort>.h5 (kind = expr | viper | immune | cna | rppa | tnfc) plus
# clinical.db and the two rppa_*.tsv sidecars. The subdirectories are frozen
# prior states and the .bak/.guardbak files are pre-edit copies: 81 MB of
# things the app never reads.
!data
data/**
!data/processed/*
# Every subdirectory of data/processed is a prior state; the app opens top-level files only.
# archive_* takes the archives whole; the */* line keeps out the contents of any other
# subdirectory, present or future. data/processed/archive_clinical_db_bak/ matched no line here
# and shipped in 0.1.7 to 0.1.9 (step 290); fixed for the class at step 291.
data/processed/archive_*
data/processed/*/*
data/processed/viper_tcga_only_backup
data/processed/*.bak
data/processed/*.bak_*
data/processed/*.pre_*
data/processed/*.guardbak

# ---- the two raw inputs that ARE runtime reads ----
# depmap: the common-essential flag (R/depmap.R). cptac: protein detectability
# (R/cptac.R). Every other data/raw/* subtree is pipeline input only. Named file by file, as
# scripts/docker_selfcheck.R section 6 names them (tests/test_release_files.R holds the two
# lists equal): data/raw/cptac/** also let through cptac_clinical.csv, which nothing reads
# (step 290, fixed at step 291). No line names the folders themselves: re-including a folder
# re-includes everything in it, which is how the CSV got through.
!data/raw/depmap/CRISPRInferredCommonEssentials.csv
!data/raw/depmap/depmap_screened_genes.txt
!data/raw/depmap/SOURCE.txt
!data/raw/cptac/cptac_proteomics.tsv.gz

# ---- ARACNe regulons ----
# The Guide states "8 tissue-specific networks" and reads the .rds files to say
# it (R/guide.R), and the candidate-regulator range comes from tf_list_*.txt.
# Shipping without them renders "0 networks" -- guide.R stops loudly instead,
# which is why these are here and the other 1.55 GB of networks/ is not.
!networks
networks/**
!networks/*/regulon_*.rds
!networks/*/tf_list_*.txt
# networks/tcga is the March 2026 TCGA-BRCA network, replaced in 0.1.8 by networks/tcga_brca
# (review item G31). No cohort's network_dir points at it any more, so it is not shipped.
networks/tcga/**

# ---- scan tables ----
# app.R's .load_scans() globs results/<cancer_type>/*.csv, top level only. The
# plots/ subdirectories are paper figures and network_concordance/ holds
# validation .rds files; neither is ever read by the app.
!results
results/**
!results/*/*.csv
results/*/archive_*

# ---- last, so no re-include above can bring them back ----
# Docker lets the LAST matching line decide. These sat at the top until 0.1.8, where
# !data/processed/* re-included Finder's data/processed/.DS_Store into the image. Step 287.
**/.DS_Store
**/.Rhistory
